{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1486697584,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyMDY2OTk1MzM=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1275","origin":"github"},"title":"publish should publish current branch (possibly even make it available on remote by default)","message":"it was kinda cool that things were actually made easier for me even while dealing with code repository:\n```shell\n(git)hopa:~/picts/mris/heudiconv[mvdoc-fixup-protocols]git\n$\u003e datalad create-sibling -s smaug smaug:proj/heudiconv\n[INFO   ] Connecting ... \nECDSA host key for IP address '129.170.233.9' not in list of known hosts.\n[INFO   ] Creating target dataset /home/yoh/picts/mris/heudiconv at proj/heudiconv \n[INFO   ] Adjusting remote git configuration \n[INFO   ] Enabling git post-update hook ... \n\n$\u003e datalad --dbg publish -r --to smaug                                                 \n[INFO   ] Publishing \u003cDataset path=/home/yoh/picts/mris/heudiconv\u003e to smaug \nECDSA host key for IP address '129.170.233.9' not in list of known hosts.\n1 item was published:\nDataset: /home/yoh/picts/mris/heudiconv\n\n```\n\nso I thought -- holy cow, I am done \"publishing\" my code to a new host... but not really since current branch wasn't pushed, not to say that it wasn't made the \"default\" one.\nI think, for a simplistic use-case, we actually might want publish to reflect current branch on the remote end... eg. in this case I would have been a happy camper right away ;)","files":null}]}